Never kill the processes holding /vendor when it is kept mounted.

ProcessResetProps() reads properties through GetPropertyFromPartition(),
which mounts /vendor, reads build.prop and unmounts it again.  On devices
that set ro.twrp.keep_vendor_mounted the unmount fails with EBUSY because
the whole Trustonic TEE stack runs from /vendor, and Unmount() then calls
KillForUseTargetProcess() to evict the holders:

  I:Killing pid 512 using '/vendor' before unmount
  I:Unable to unmount '/vendor'

The killed process was mcDriverDaemon.  Losing it resets the secure world
mid-startup, init restarts the KeyMint HAL against a dirty TEE and its
trustlet open fails with NO_FREE_INSTANCES, so /data never gets decrypted
("Unable to decrypt metadata encryption").  When the daemon is started
late instead - after that window - KeyMint loads tlTeeKeymint_rpmb and
serves TEE_ComputeSharedMac normally.

Skip the eviction for /vendor when the mount is meant to stay.

diff --git a/twrp_functions.cpp b/twrp_functions.cpp
index 207691c..2155e10 100644
--- a/twrp_functions.cpp
+++ b/twrp_functions.cpp
@@ -210,6 +210,19 @@ void TWFunc::KillForUseTargetProcess(const std::string& target) {
 
   std::string directory = target;
   while (directory.size() > 1 && directory.back() == '/') directory.pop_back();
+
+  // Devices that keep /vendor mounted on purpose run the whole TEE stack
+  // (mcDriverDaemon, KeyMint, Gatekeeper) from there, so they always hold files
+  // under it.  Unmounting then fails with EBUSY and this helper would kill those
+  // daemons: the secure world resets, the KeyMint trustlet instance is leaked
+  // and FBE decryption becomes impossible.  The mount is not going away, so
+  // there is nothing to evict.
+  if (directory == "/vendor" &&
+      android::base::GetBoolProperty("ro.twrp.keep_vendor_mounted", false)) {
+    LOGINFO("Keeping processes using '/vendor' alive (ro.twrp.keep_vendor_mounted)\n");
+    return;
+  }
+
   const std::string prefix = directory == "/" ? directory : directory + "/";
 
   std::string output;
